En Macédoine, en 2001, l''armée engage hélicoptères Mi-24 et avions Su-25 contre la guérilla albanaise ; des Su-25 effectuent le 23 juin les premières reconnaissances au-dessus d''Aračinovo. L''accord d''Ohrid du 13 août 2001 clôt ce dernier conflit, sans engagement des appareils du catalogue.', 'In 1991 the federal air force waged war against opponents with almost no aircraft. In Slovenia it struck Brnik airport on 28 June and the transmitters carrying the government''s broadcasts, but lost two helicopters as early as 27 June. In Croatia it supported ground troops, notably at Vukovar, and on 7 October two MiG-21s and two G-4s struck Banski dvori in Zagreb two or three minutes after Presidents Tuđman and Mesić and federal Prime Minister Marković had left the dining room; none was hurt. Croatian guns and shoulder-launched missiles brought down several Jastrebs and an Orao; according to Wikipedia, the federal air force lost 46 aircraft and helicopters in Slovenia, Croatia and Bosnia in 1991-92.

