Les insurgés n''ont pas d''aviation. Le 1er janvier 1964, la RAF aligne à Khormaksar 96 appareils, selon l''historique de la base : trois escadrons de chasseurs-bombardiers Hunter, des Shackleton, des hélicoptères Belvedere, des transports Beverley, Argosy, Twin Pioneer et Valetta. L''Army Air Corps opère depuis Falaise, à Little Aden, et les porte-avions de la Royal Navy font escale au large. La guerre civile qui se déroule au même moment au Yémen du Nord a sa propre page (« Guerre civile yéménite »).', 'A British colony since 1839, Aden was home in the 1960s to Middle East Command and to RAF Khormaksar, the busiest and most crowded station in the RAF. London had joined the colony and the hinterland emirates into a Federation of South Arabia, but the 1962 republican revolution in North Yemen, backed by Nasser''s Egypt, gave nationalists a safe haven across the border. On 14 October 1963, Radfan tribesmen attacked British troops. On 10 December, a grenade thrown at High Commissioner Sir Kennedy Trevaskis on the Khormaksar tarmac killed his assistant George Henderson and a bystander, and a state of emergency was declared across South Arabia.

